From b39015e04b7ebaed94dd600671671c315f245e0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:59:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build on macOS 10.5 and 10.6

- Detect big-endian targets instead of hardcoding little-endian, which
  broke Iridas .look parsing on PowerPC.
- Monitor ICC profiles: CGDisplayCreateUUIDFromDisplayID is 10.7+, so use
  CMGetProfileByAVID and NCMGetProfileLocation, which exist for both
  32-bit and 64-bit on 10.5 and 10.6.
- ColorSync and CoreGraphics are not top-level frameworks before 10.8;
  include and link ApplicationServices instead.
- Add OCIO_METAL_ENABLED (default OFF) to gate the Metal backend.
- Add OCIO_USE_APPLE_GL (default ON) to choose between the system
  OpenGL/GLUT frameworks and GLEW/freeglut, exported from oglapphelpers
  so the apps and GPU tests see it.
- With the system frameworks, use EXT_framebuffer_object and
  GL_LUMINANCE32F_ARB, which GL 2.x renderers on 10.5/10.6 provide;
  the 10.5 SDK lacks ARB_framebuffer_object and ARB_texture_rg.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
